[RUNTIME] src/code_forge/cli.py:920-920 - The new 'truncated' flag is computed from st.st_size before the file is opened. A concurrent writer, editor, build process, or git checkout can change the file between stat() and open()/read(). If the file grows after stat, 'truncated' is False and read_text() can emit more than the 50KB cap with no truncation marker; if it shrinks after stat, 'truncated' is True and a complete short read is marked as truncated. No lock or snapshot protects the call. Smoke test: run _assemble_post_image while another process appends/truncates the target file, then verify the marker and byte count match the bytes actually read.
[RUNTIME] src/code_forge/cli.py:854-854 - The new guard drops hunks whose start is past the line count of the text actually read. hunk_map comes from a diff generated earlier and is not locked to the file state, so a stale hunk can be silently discarded if the working-tree file is shorter than the diff's post-image (concurrent edit, partial checkout, or the 50KB truncation). The fallback 'if not wanted' then returns the whole file unwindowed, or only sibling windows, so a real change may not be marked as 'around the changes'. Smoke test: feed a stale hunk_map with start > current line count plus a valid sibling hunk; verify the valid hunk is shown and the stale hunk does not widen the window.
[RUNTIME] src/code_forge/cli.py:939-939 - The truncation marker is now appended after _window_file_text, so it is no longer a line in the text passed to windowing and is always present even in a windowed excerpt. This changes the generated markdown the CLI emits: downstream parsers or consumers that expected the marker only in unwindowed output or at a specific line offset will see different text. Also, when the hunk windows cover every line of the truncated partial read, _window_file_text now returns windowed=False, so the label changes from '... (around the changes)' to the plain filename. Smoke test: assemble post-image for >50KB files with hunks before, at, and after the cap; verify marker placement, labels, and that gap counts never exceed the file length.
